<https://w3id.org/lmodel/stix/stix> dcterms:license "Apache-2.0" ;
	dcterms:source "https://docs.oasis-open.org/cti/stix/v2.1/os/stix-v2.1-os.html"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	dcterms:title "Structured Threat Information Expression (STIX)" ;
	pav:version "2.1" ;
	a linkml:SchemaDefinition ;
	rdfs:seeAlso "https://github.com/oasis-open/cti-stix2-json-schemas/tree/9af1db41b7b86c06324f899649ae83480134f66e"^^xsd:anyURI , "https://lmodel.github.io/stix"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	skos:note "Classes and slots map to terms of the Unified Cyber Ontology (UCO) 1.5.0 where the meaning matches, under UCO's own namespaces: close_mappings for the cyber-observable objects, their extensions and the shared objects, and broad_mappings for Tool, which UCO defines more widely. The domain objects that UCO has no term for are left unmapped. tests/test_mappings.py checks each against UCO's term list." , "The JSON keys that contain a hyphen are dictionary keys, never property names: hash algorithms (SHA-256), extension names (ntfs-ext) and extension definition identifiers. The dictionaries that hold them are classes with extra_slots, which the generated JSON Schema checks; the generated Python models do not, and docs/index.md lists what goes unchecked." , "The classes are closed: an object validates only with the properties its class declares. STIX allows custom properties and custom objects; they validate once a schema that imports this one declares them, as a slot of a subclass or a class of its own, as lmodel/attack does for MITRE's x_mitre_ properties and x-mitre- objects. Opening the object bases with extra_slots would accept every misspelled key as well, and LinkML 1.12.1's Pydantic generator ignores extra_slots." , "The specification is copyright OASIS Open, and nothing here copies its text. Descriptions come from OASIS's JSON schemas, which are under the BSD-3-Clause licence that NOTICE carries, or are this project's own." , "The version is the edition of STIX that the schema renders, and source is the OASIS Standard of 10 June 2021. OASIS publishes no release of its JSON schemas, so upstream/ copies them, their examples and their licence at the commit in the annotations, and scripts/check_upstream_release.py reports when that repository moves. STIX 2.1 Errata 01 exists only as a Committee Specification Draft (2 April 2025); the schema follows the approved standard, and the values the draft adds to four open vocabularies validate anyway." ;
